 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch37_04_01\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idm190917760\" data-alt=\"The hypothalamus secretes thyrotropin-releasing hormone, which causes the anterior pituitary gland to secrete thyroid-stimulating hormone. Thyroid-stimulating hormone causes the thyroid gland to secrete the thyroid hormones T3 and T4, which increase metabolism, resulting in growth and development. In a negative feedback loop, T3 and T4 inhibit hormone secretion by the hypothalamus and pituitary, terminating the signal.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20210823.155019/resources/574107daaac72faebf16f0f3b53297f929af9815\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"The hypothalamus secretes thyrotropin-releasing hormone, which causes the anterior pituitary gland to secrete thyroid-stimulating hormone. Thyroid-stimulating hormone causes the thyroid gland to secrete the thyroid hormones T3 and T4, which increase metabolism, resulting in growth and development. In a negative feedback loop, T3 and T4 inhibit hormone secretion by the hypothalamus and pituitary, terminating the signal.\" width=\"280\" id=\"3\">\n</span>\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 241924,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/bd23c90667727d65.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Adhi N. Sharma and D. L. Levy/Semantic Scholar)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>Study the given feedback loop.</p>\n<p>Which of the given relationships would hold true?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 757158,
     "content_html": "TSH increases production of TRH."
    },
    {
     "id": 757157,
     "content_html": "TSH decreases production of T3."
    },
    {
     "id": 757156,
     "content_html": "T3 increases production ot T4."
    },
    {
     "id": 757159,
     "content_html": "T4 decreases production of TRH."
    }
